## General eligibility criteria for CAP/DA under NC Medicaid

Under **Clinical Coverage Policy 3K-2**, a person is generally eligible for **CAP/DA** if they meet the following requirements:

### Basic Medicaid eligibility
The beneficiary must:
- be **enrolled in the NC Medicaid Program**; and
- not have **service restrictions due to their eligibility category** that make them ineligible for CAP/DA.

**Citation:** Policy **3K-2**, Section **sec:doc:clinical_policy:3K-2:2.1.1** (effective date not listed in section; authoritative document effective **2025-09-01**; no amendments returned).

### CAP/DA-specific criteria
NC Medicaid covers CAP/DA when the beneficiary:
- **meets the required HCBS nursing facility level of care (LOC)** as determined by NC Medicaid;
- **requires long-term care support at a level typically provided in an institution**, and that need is directly related to a documented medical diagnosis and functional care need;
- has a **completed CAP assessment** showing a reasonable indication they will need at least one CAP/DA HCBS service within **30 calendar days** of the evaluation;
- has a **signed service plan** authorizing one or more waiver services on a monthly basis, or short-term equipment/modification/technology to help the person return to or remain in the home and avoid institutional placement;
- is **able to maintain health, safety, and well-being** in the primary private residence or approved location with **formal and informal supports**;
- has paid care needs that can be maintained **within the average institutional cost of the CAP/DA waiver**;
- has a **primary physician** who can link and coordinate medical services; and
- has an **emergency back-up and disaster plan**.

**Citation:** Policy **3K-2**, Section **sec:doc:clinical_policy:3K-2:3.2.1** (authoritative document effective **2025-09-01**; no amendments returned).

### Additional general waiver-entry criteria
Another section of the same policy states that, for Medicaid CAP/DA participation, the person:
- is enrolled in **fee-for-service (Medicaid Direct)**;
- is determined to require a **level of institutional care under the NC State Medicaid Plan**;
- is a member of a **target group documented in the approved waiver application**;
- meets applicable Medicaid eligibility criteria in **Section 2.1.2b**;
- **exercises freedom of choice** to enter or remain in the waiver;
- is assigned a **CAP/DA waiver slot**;
- is able to maintain health, safety, and well-being at home or an approved location with formal and informal supports; and
- is **age 18 or older**.

**Citation:** Policy **3K-2**, Section **sec:doc:clinical_policy:3K-2:_s17** (“a. Medicaid”) (authoritative document effective **2025-09-01**; no amendments returned).

## Plain-language summary
In plain English, **CAP/DA is for adults on NC Medicaid who need a nursing-facility level of care, but can safely stay at home or in another approved setting if waiver services and supports are in place**. They must also be in **Medicaid Direct**, have a **CAP assessment**, a **service plan**, a **waiver slot**, and be able to stay safely in the community with both paid and unpaid supports.

